---
title: "Applied Music – Keyboard"
code: "MUS-145"
category: "music"
credits: "1"
prerequisites: []
corequisites: []
---

Teaches piano, organ, harpsichord, or synthesizer. Studies the standard repertoire. Private lessons are available for either 1 or 2 hours of credit per semester. The length of the lessons will be 1/2 hour for 1 hour credit. All courses in applied music may be repeated for a total of 8 hours for the major and 4 hours for the minor. 1 half-hour lessons per week, 4 hours practice (laboratory) required. Laboratory 4 hours. Total 4 hours per week.
